      "q": "(i) Write about components of theodolite 6 1 (ii) Write down the process of getting horizontal angle with the help of theodolite. 9 1",
      "answer": "1. THEODOLITE OVERVIEW:\nA theodolite is a precision instrument used for measuring both horizontal and vertical angles in surveying and triangulation networks.\n\n2. CORE COMPONENTS & FUNCTIONS:\n• Telescope: Internal focusing telescope with cross-hair diaphragm for sighting target stations.\n• Vertical & Horizontal Circles: Graduated glass/metal circles equipped with verniers or optical micrometers to read angles up to 20\" or 1\".\n• Level Tubes (Plate & Altitude Bubbles): Sensitive spirit levels used for precise horizontal and vertical leveling.\n• Upper & Lower Plates: Lower plate carries the graduated horizontal limb; upper plate carries the verniers and standards.\n• Levelling Head (Tribrach & Trivet): Three foot-screws for leveling the instrument on the tripod stand.\n\n3. FIELD ADJUSTMENTS:\n• Temporary adjustments: Setting up, leveling using foot-screws, and elimination of parallax.\n• Permanent adjustments: Plate level axis perpendicular to vertical axis; line of collimation perpendicular to horizontal axis.",
