      "year": 2025,
      "marks": 15,
      "group": "Group C",
      "topic": "Exam Paper 2025 (18)",
      "q": "a) Derive the Major Principal Stress and the plane at which maximum tangential stress occurs considering a 2D Stress system. (10) b) Analyse and draw the Shear Force Diagram & Bending Moment Diagram for the Simply Supported Beam shown in Fig. 1. Label all the necessary values of SF and BM in the diagrams. (5)",
      "answer": "1. PRINCIPAL STRESSES & PLANES:\nPrincipal planes are planes on which the shear stress is identically zero. The normal stresses acting on these planes are termed Principal Stresses (σ1 and σ2).\n\n2. ANALYTICAL FORMULATION:\nFor a 2D stress state (σx, σy, τxy):\n• Major Principal Stress: σ1 = (σx + σy)/2 + √[((σx - σy)/2)² + τxy²]\n• Minor Principal Stress: σ2 = (σx + σy)/2 - √[((σx - σy)/2)² + τxy²]\n• Maximum Shear Stress: τmax = (σ1 - σ2)/2 = √[((σx - σy)/2)² + τxy²]\n• Principal Plane Orientation: tan(2θp) = 2τxy / (σx - σy)\n\n3. MOHR'S CIRCLE CONSTRUCTION:\n• Center of circle: C = ((σx + σy)/2, 0)\n• Radius of circle: R = √[((σx - σy)/2)² + τxy²] = τmax\n• Point (σx, -τxy) and (σy, +τxy) define the diameter endpoints.",
      "keyPoints": [
        "Definition of principal plane (zero shear stress)",
        "Formulae for major (σ1), minor (σ2), and maximum shear stress (τmax)",
        "Mohr's circle center and radius coordinates"
      ],
