      "q": "(i) State any four points of differentiation between compile time polymorphism and run time polymorphism with valid example. 5 4 4 (ii) What is the advantage of exception handling? Difference between exception and error. 5 3 2 (iii) Mention the differences between constructor and destructor with suitable example. 5 5 2",
      "answer": "1. EXCEPTION HANDLING MECHANISM IN C++:\nException handling provides a structured way to separate error detection from error handling, preventing abrupt program termination.\n\n2. CORE KEYWORDS:\n• try block: Encloses code that might generate an error.\n• throw expression: Sends an exception object when an anomaly is detected.\n• catch block: Intercepts and resolves the exception.\n\n3. CODE EXAMPLE:\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\ndouble divide(double num, double den) {\n    if (den == 0) throw \"Error: Division by zero!\";\n    return num / den;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    try {\n        cout << divide(10, 2) << endl;\n        cout << divide(5, 0) << endl;\n    } catch (const char* msg) {\n        cerr << msg << endl;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n4. ADVANTAGES: Clean error reporting, stack unwinding ensures local object destructors are invoked.",
