      "answer": "1. MATHEMATICAL FORMULATION & ALGORITHM:\nNumerical and statistical techniques approximate analytical solutions with controlled truncation and roundoff error tolerances.\n\n2. STEP-BY-STEP NUMERICAL PROCEDURE:\n• Root Finding (Newton-Raphson): Iteration formula x_{n+1} = x_n - [f(x_n) / f'(x_n)]. Quadratic rate of convergence (|e_{n+1}| ≈ k |e_n|²).\n• System of Equations (Gauss-Seidel / SOR): Successive displacement method where updated coordinates are immediately substituted into subsequent row equations. Requires diagonal dominance for guaranteed convergence (|a_ii| > ∑|a_ij|).\n• Numerical Integration (Simpson's Rules): Approximates integrand with parabolas over subintervals (h/3 rule for even intervals).\n\n3. ERROR ANALYSIS & CONVERGENCE:\nStopping criteria: |x_{n+1} - x_n| < ε (e.g., 10⁻³ or 10⁻⁴). Truncation error bounded by Taylor series expansion remainder.",
