      "answer": "1. PROCESS FUNDAMENTALS:\nIn manufacturing technology, casting, forming, and welding represent primary shaping processes governed by thermal, metallurgical, and mechanical principles.\n\n2. DETAILED TECHNICAL ANALYSIS:\n• Gating System / Tooling: Sprues are tapered downwards to maintain continuous fluid contact and prevent air aspiration (Bernoulli & Continuity equations: A1·v1 = A2·v2).\n• Pattern Allowances: Shrinkage/contraction allowance, draft allowance for easy pattern withdrawal, machining allowance, and distortion allowance.\n• Defects & Remedies:\n  - Blow holes / porosity: Provide adequate sand permeability and venting holes.\n  - Cold shuts / misruns: Increase pouring temperature and modify gating size.\n  - Flash / cold cracks: Ensure proper die alignment and pre-heating.\n\n3. INDUSTRIAL APPLICATION:\nCrucial for mass production of automotive engine blocks, forged crankshafts, and pressure vessels complying with ASME and BIS standards.",
