      "q": "State the Rule of Mixtures in composite materials. Derive the formula for longitudinal elastic modulus (E1) of a unidirectional continuous fiber-reinforced composite.",
      "answer": "1. RULE OF MIXTURES:\nThe rule of mixtures is a mathematical method for estimating the overall mechanical properties of a composite material based on the volume fractions of its constituents (fiber and matrix).\n\n2. DERIVATION FOR LONGITUDINAL MODULUS (E1 - ISOSTRAIN CONDITION):\nAssume equal strain in fiber and matrix under longitudinal tensile load: ε1 = εf = εm.\nTotal applied load P = Pf + Pm = σf·Af + σm·Am.\nDividing by total cross-sectional area A:\nσ1 = σf·(Af/A) + σm·(Am/A) = σf·Vf + σm·Vm.\nSince σ = E·ε:\nE1·ε1 = Ef·εf·Vf + Em·εm·Vm.\nCanceling equal strains ε1 = εf = εm:\nE1 = Ef·Vf + Em·Vm, where Vm = 1 - Vf.",
