      "q": "State Euler's formula for connected planar graphs. Prove that for any simple connected planar graph with v ≥ 3 vertices and e edges, e ≤ 3v - 6.",
      "answer": "1. EULER'S FORMULA FOR PLANAR GRAPHS:\nFor any connected planar graph drawn without edge crossings with v vertices, e edges, and f faces (including the unbounded exterior face):\nv - e + f = 2.\n\n2. PROOF OF e ≤ 3v - 6:\n• Every face in a simple planar graph is bounded by at least 3 edges (since simple graphs have no self-loops or parallel edges).\n• Each edge separates at most two faces, so taking the sum of degrees of all faces gives: 2e = ∑ deg(F_i) ≥ 3f.\n• Thus: f ≤ (2/3)e.\n• Substituting this into Euler's formula:\nv - e + (2/3)e ≥ 2\nv - (1/3)e ≥ 2\n(1/3)e ≤ v - 2\ne ≤ 3v - 6.\n\n3. APPLICATION:\nUsed to prove that K5 (complete graph with 5 vertices, v=5, e=10) is non-planar since 10 ≤ 3(5) - 6 = 9 is FALSE.",
