      "q": "Solve the recurrence relation a_n - 7a_{n-1} + 10a_{n-2} = 0 with initial conditions a_0 = 1, a_1 = 8 using characteristic roots and generating functions.",
      "answer": "1. CHARACTERISTIC EQUATION METHOD:\nThe characteristic equation is:\nr² - 7r + 10 = 0\n(r - 2)(r - 5) = 0\nRoots: r1 = 2, r2 = 5 (distinct real roots).\n\nGeneral Solution:\na_n = C1·(2)^n + C2·(5)^n.\n\nApplying Initial Conditions:\n• For n = 0: a_0 = C1·(1) + C2·(1) = C1 + C2 = 1 ⇒ C2 = 1 - C1\n• For n = 1: a_1 = C1·(2) + C2·(5) = 2C1 + 5(1 - C1) = 5 - 3C1 = 8\n-3C1 = 3 ⇒ C1 = -1\nC2 = 1 - (-1) = 2.\n\nFinal Particular Solution:\na_n = -1·(2)^n + 2·(5)^n = 2·(5)^n - (2)^n.\n\nVerification:\na_0 = 2·1 - 1 = 1 (Correct)\na_1 = 2·5 - 2 = 8 (Correct)\na_2 = 7(8) - 10(1) = 46. Formula: 2·25 - 4 = 46 (Verified).",
