      "q": "Define Poisson distribution. State its probability mass function (PMF), mean, variance, and the conditions under which Binomial distribution tends to Poisson distribution.",
      "answer": "1. POISSON DISTRIBUTION PMF:\nA discrete random variable X follows a Poisson distribution with parameter λ > 0 if:\nP(X = k) = (e^(-λ) · λ^k) / k!, where k = 0, 1, 2, ...\n\n2. STATISTICAL PROPERTIES:\n• Mean E[X] = λ\n• Variance Var(X) = λ (Mean equals Variance)\n• Standard deviation σ = √λ\n\n3. LIMITING CASE OF BINOMIAL DISTRIBUTION (POISSON APPROXIMATION):\nA Binomial distribution B(n, p) approaches Poisson distribution P(λ) under three conditions:\n• The number of trials n → ∞ (infinitely large).\n• The probability of success p → 0 (very rare event).\n• The product np = λ remains constant (finite positive value).",
